## Combining Overlays

Multiple overlays can be rendered together by passing them through the `overlays` property.

```tsx
import { ClassifiedChart } from "classifiedlens";

const candles = [
  { time: 1710000000, open: 100, high: 105, low: 98, close: 103 },
  { time: 1710000300, open: 103, high: 108, low: 101, close: 106 },
  { time: 1710000600, open: 106, high: 109, low: 104, close: 105 },
];

const overlays = [
  {
    id: "support",
    kind: "horizontal_line",
    price: 100,
    title: "Support",
  },
  {
    id: "resistance",
    kind: "horizontal_line",
    price: 110,
    title: "Resistance",
  },
  {
    id: "entry",
    kind: "marker",
    time: 1710000300,
    position: "belowBar",
    shape: "arrowUp",
    text: "Entry",
  },
  {
    id: "target",
    kind: "trade_level",
    levelType: "take_profit",
    price: 115,
    title: "Target",
  },
];

export default function App() {
  return (
    <div style={{ width: "100%", height: 600 }}>
      <ClassifiedChart data={candles} overlays={overlays} />
    </div>
  );
}
```

## Chart Configuration

ClassifiedLens supports four chart modes:

- `standard`
- `trading`
- `analysis`
- `replay`

Chart configuration can be passed through the `configuration` property.

```tsx
const configuration = {
  mode: "analysis",
  dimensions: {
    height: 600,
    minHeight: 300,
  },
  options: {},
  timeScale: {},
};

<ClassifiedChart
  data={candles}
  configuration={configuration}
  overlays={overlays}
/>;
```

## Overlay Layers

Overlays can optionally specify a rendering layer:

- `background`
- `structure`
- `signal`
- `trade`
- `annotation`
- `foreground`

Example:

```tsx
const overlay = {
  id: "entry",
  kind: "marker",
  layer: "signal",
  time: 1710000300,
  position: "belowBar",
  shape: "arrowUp",
};
```

## Overlay Metadata

Overlays can contain application-defined metadata.

```tsx
const overlay = {
  id: "liquidity-level",
  kind: "horizontal_line",
  price: 105,
  title: "Liquidity",
  metadata: {
    source: "my-application",
    category: "swing-high",
  },
};
```

ClassifiedLens preserves metadata without interpreting its application-specific meaning.

